366140.literal_statement:
Fix nonnegative integers $x_1,\dots,x_{16}$ with $x_1+\dots+x_8=n$. Let $\mathcal{S}_{\mathbf{x}}$ be the collection of all quadruples $(\mathcal{A}_1,\dots,\mathcal{A}_4)$ whose sixteen overlap sizes are $x_1,\dots,x_{16}$; let $\mathcal{A}_i'$ denote the complementary set associated with $\mathcal{A}_i$, and let $\operatorname{sgn}(\sigma_{\mathcal{A}_i})$ and $\Delta_{\mathcal{A}_i}$ have the meanings used for the corresponding Vandermonde terms. **Vandermonde-sum conjecture.** One has

$$
\begin{aligned}
&\sum_{(\mathcal{A}_1,\dots,\mathcal{A}_4)\subset \mathcal{S}_{\mathbf{x}}} \prod_{i=1}^4 \operatorname{sgn}(\sigma_{\mathcal{A}_i})\Delta_{\mathcal{A}_i}^2\Delta_{\mathcal{A}_i'}^2 \\
&\qquad=\mathbf{1}(x_i=x_{17-i})\,(-1)^{x_2+x_3+x_5+x_7}\binom{n}{x_1,\dots,x_8}
\sum_{\substack{\mathcal{A}\subset [\![2n]\!],\\ |\mathcal{A}|=n}}\Delta_{\mathcal{A}}^4\Delta_{\mathcal{A}'}^4.
\end{aligned}
$$

This is proposed as a generalization of the established Cauchy-cycle identity and is motivated by the exchangeability-based reduction of fourth moments of determinants.

